    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "h",
      "level": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Structural Divergence"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The current picture shows two different timeframes playing out in parallel. In the short term, selling dominates and the price pulls back. In the medium term, three independent sources paint a bullish staircase: a breakout above "
        },
        {
          "text": "$85,000",
          "bold": true,
          "color": "green"
        },
        {
          "text": ", an advance to "
        },
        {
          "text": "$93,000",
          "bold": true,
          "color": "green"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and in the background, the thesis of a structurally positive season."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "This type of divergence often marks accumulation zones. When the price pulls back but the outlook from analysts and institutional managers improves, the tendency is for either sentiment to adjust to price or price to adjust to sentiment — depending on which side gives in first."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "h",
      "level": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "What to Watch"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The first reference point is "
        },
        {
          "text": "Bitcoin's",
          "bold": true
        },
        {
          "text": " reaction if it retests the "
        },
        {
          "text": "$80,000",
          "bold": true
        },
        {
          "text": " region. Buying at that level would reinforce the bullish staircase thesis. Selling that pushes the price below that level would invalidate the short-term scenario."
